    "extracted text": "The reactants used to prepare IM-16 were TEOS (>98% Fluka), Aerosil 200 (>98% Degussa), amorphous germanium oxide GeO2 (>99.99%, Aldrich), HF acid (40%, Carlo Erba), distilled water, and 3-ethyl-1-methyl-3H-imidazol-1-ium bromide (98%, Solvionic), which was transformed into its OH form by ion exchange in water (Dowex SBR LC NG, OH Form (Supelco)). The OSDA solutions were concentrated by lyophilisation when necessary. All the syntheses were performed in 2 mL Teflon-lined autoclaves at 170 °C for 14 days. Silica sources: a TEOS (tetraethylorthosilicate), b Aerosil 200. c Argutite. d ε?: small quantity of one or more unknown impurities. e Quartz.",
    
    "property mapping": "H2O/T - Water to total T atoms (T = Si + Ge) ratio\nR/T - OSDA (3-ethyl-1-methyl-3H-imidazol-1-ium) to total T atoms ratio\nHF/T - Fluoride to total T atoms ratio\nSi/Ge - Silicon to Germanium ratio\nT - Total framework atoms (Si + Ge)",
    
    "formula abbreviations": "T = Si + Ge (total framework atoms)\nR = 3-ethyl-1-methyl-3H-imidazol-1-ium (OSDA)\nε? = small quantity of one or more unknown impurities\nQ = Quartz\nArg = Argutite",
    
    "ratio calculations": "For each recipe, we need to set Si to 1.0 and adjust other ratios accordingly.\nGiven Si/Ge ratio and total T atoms (Si + Ge = 1), we can calculate:\nSi + Ge = 1\nSi/(Si + Ge) = Si/T = Si ratio in the gel\nGe/(Si + Ge) = Ge/T = Ge ratio in the gel\n\nFor example, for sample 16b with Si/Ge = 0.5:0.5:\nSi = 0.5, Ge = 0.5\nSetting Si to 1.0: Ge = 0.5/0.5 = 1.0\nR/T = 1.0, so OSDA ratio = 1.0 * (Si + Ge)/Si = 1.0 * (0.5 + 0.5)/0.5 = 2.0\nH2O/T = 20, so H2O ratio = 20 * (Si + Ge)/Si = 20 * (0.5 + 0.5)/0.5 = 40.0\nHF/T = 1.0, so HF ratio = 1.0 * (Si + Ge)/Si = 1.0 * (0.5 + 0.5)/0.5 = 2.0",
    
